*** Settings ***
Library  user_message_subscriber.py



*** Keywords ***
Register callback
        [Documentation]     Use keyword to add callback to observer.
        ...                 Callback func must be decorated with @message_verifier decarator
        ...                 and must take as input (owner_alias, unparsed_owner_message) pararms.
        ...                 Must be used after the Observe* keyword has been invoked.
        ...                 subscriber_owner_alias option can be used only when Observe* keyword also included
        ...                 ${subscriber_owner_alias} option.
        [Arguments]         ${message_type}        ${callback}      ${subscriber_owner_alias}=${None}
        user single message subscriber register user callback
        ...    ${message_type}
        ...    ${callback}
        ...    owner_alias=${subscriber_owner_alias}


Register verifier
        [Documentation]     Use keyword to add verifier to observer. Verifier (if at least one fails) rejects given
        ...                 message occurence, which is not being stored and callbacks are not executed for
        ...                 that occurence.
        ...                 Should be used as message pre-filter but only if really needed.
        ...                 Callback func must be decorated with @message_verifier decarator
        ...                 and must take as input SINGLE param (message).
        ...                 Also query language syntax can be used.
        ...                 Must be used after the Observe* keyword has been invoked.
        ...                 subscriber_owner_alias option can be used only when Observe* keyword also included
        ...                 ${subscriber_owner_alias} option.
        ...                 Note: It impacts fast-occcuring messages performance, as callback need to decode each
        ...                 message from byte form to ASN form in order to execute query
        [Arguments]         ${message_type}        ${verifier}      ${subscriber_owner_alias}=${None}
        user single message subscriber register user verifier
        ...    ${message_type}
        ...    ${verifier}
        ...    owner_alias=${subscriber_owner_alias}

Observe ${message_type:\S+} for indefinite time
        [Documentation]     Use to start observer for single message type, disregarding owner.
        ...                 Observer runs indefinitely, so only reasonable usage is together with Register callback
        ...                 keyword to get any value from the captured messages.
        user_single_message_subscriber_subscribe
        ...   ${message_type}


Observe ${message_type:\S+} for ${timeout:\d+}s
        [Documentation]     Use it for single message, diregarding the owner for given timeout.
        ...                 Observer will always catch for entire ${timeout} time, so when Get awaited* keyword
        ...                 is used, it will block until timeout ends.
        user_single_message_subscriber_subscribe
        ...   ${message_type}
        ...   ${timeout}

Observe ${message_type:\S+} for ${num:\d+} occurrences for ${timeout:\d+}s
        [Documentation]     Use it for single message, diregarding the owner for given timeout.
        ...                 Observer will catch for entire ${timeout} time but only until given number of messages is captured.
        ...                 So when Get awaited* keyword is used, it may block until timeout ends or until given
        ...                 number of messages are captured.
        ...                 Note: If the timeout occurs and at least one message was caucht but the ${num} condition is not
        ...                 fullfilled, it will not fail, only return the captured messages (if !=0).
        ...                 If want to fail a test, in Get awaited* keyword use the occurrences param
        user_single_message_subscriber_subscribe
        ...   ${message_type}
        ...   ${timeout}
        ...   ${num}


Observe ${message_type:\S+} for ${num:\d+} occurrences for ${timeout:\d+}s for owner ${subscriber_owner_alias:\S+}
        [Documentation]     Use it for single message, ONLY for the given owner.
        ...                 Observer will catch for entire ${timeout} time but only until given number of messages is captured.
        ...                 So when Get awaited* keyword is used, it may block until timeout ends or until given
        ...                 number of messages are captured.
        ...                 Note: to use Get awaited* or Register callback keyword, must also provide ${subscriber_owner_alias}
        ...                 option.
        user_single_message_subscriber_subscribe
        ...   ${message_type}
        ...   ${timeout}
        ...   ${num}
        ...   owner_alias=${subscriber_owner_alias}


Get awaited messages
        [Documentation]       Use this keyword to wait and/or retrieve messages from started observer.
        ...                   It is meant to be used with timeout or count observer.
        ...                   It cannot be used with indefinite observer.
        ...                   It blocks until timeout/message count is received.
        ...                   In case n messages were requested and n-1 was caught, where n-1 > 0, it will not fail and
        ...                   will return n-1 messages.
        ...                   occurrences param can be used to verify that requested number of messages was captured.
        ...                   It returns unparsed messages or parsed, depending on ${parsed} param.
        ...                   Can be used multiple times until next 'Observe' keyword is called.
        ...
        ...                   If NO owner_alias NOR subscriber_owner_alias is provided:
        ...                   - returns all messages messages from observer, disregarding owner.
        ...                   If owner_alias is provided (without subscriber_owner_alias):
        ...                   - returns all messages messages from observer for given owner.
        ...                   If owner_alias is provided together with subscriber_owner_alias:
        ...                   - returns all messages messages from observer for given owner
        ...                   - can be used only when Observe* keyword was also used with subscriber_owner_alias
        ...
        ...                   Returns messages only from current/last observer.
        ...                   For python verification of messages use
        ...                   from ta_messaging.user_message_subscriber import get_messages_from_subscriber
        [Arguments]  ${message_type}    ${parsed}=${FALSE}   ${owner_alias}=${None}    ${subscriber_owner_alias}=${None}
        ...          ${occurrences}=${None}
        ${msgs}=     get_messages_from_subscriber
        ...     ${message_type}
        ...     parsed=${parsed}
        ...     owner_alias=${owner_alias}
        ...     subscriber_owner_alias=${subscriber_owner_alias}
        ...     occurrences=${occurrences}
        [Return]        ${msgs}
